# What must not be versioned, and why.
#
# This mirrors the exclusion list in scripts/package-submission.ps1, which is the
# list the submission ZIP has been built and checked against. Keeping the two in
# step matters: a repository that disagrees with the shipped archive is a second,
# quieter definition of "the project", and the first thing a reviewer would notice
# is that cloning gives them something the ZIP does not (or the reverse).
#
# The rule is: source, docs, tests and the evidence the documents reference are
# versioned; anything that is a cache, a dependency, a clone or a build output is
# not, because every one of them is reproducible from the tracked files.
# scripts/setup.ps1 fetches the rest.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments — a "# ..." after a pattern becomes part
# of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing. Every comment is its own line.

# --- third-party clone and dependency trees (fetched, not vendored) ---
# ~985 MB Agnes Harness checkout; setup.ps1 clones it
_agh_src/
agh_docs/
# ~344 MB of wheels; setup.ps1 installs them
.pylibs/
.venv/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-home/
.npm-cache/
.corepack/
.node-headers/
data/node-headers/
.piptmp/

# --- raw data caches, all re-downloadable by the scripts ---
# Copernicus DEM GLO-30 tiles
data/dem/
# ESA WorldCover tiles
data/landcover/
# OpenStreetMap extracts
data/osm/
# Open-Meteo response cache
data/weather/

# --- scratch and machine-local state ---
data/tmp/
# matplotlib font cache
.mplconfig/
# the AGH profile written by 启动AGH.cmd
.agh-home/
.acl-recovery/
# per-machine paths written by setup.ps1
.floodkit.json

# --- build output and the mutation-testing scratch trees ---
# the submission ZIP is a build artifact, not source
dist/
_mutation/
_cleanroom/
_zipview/

# --- the organisers' competition notice: their document, not this project's output ---
/关于举办*

# --- derived files that must never ride along, wherever they land ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.npy
*.part
*.log
